# One line-ending convention everywhere: LF in the repository.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Dockerfile.runner and the scripts the sandbox path touches are
# executed inside a Linux container; a CRLF line ending there produces failures that look
# like the script is wrong rather than the checkout ("\r: command not found", a shebang
# that resolves to nothing). Normalising here rules that class of bug out before the
# sandbox's first real run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must be LF regardless of platform, because Linux executes them.
Dockerfile        text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*      text eol=lf
*.sh              text eol=lf
*.py              text eol=lf
*.yaml            text eol=lf
*.yml             text eol=lf

# PowerShell is Windows-side only and CRLF is its native convention.
*.ps1             text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png             binary
*.jpg             binary
*.ico             binary
*.pdf             binary
*.vhdx            binary
